Nell McLaughlin, played by Geraldine Wall.

10
00:52:21,176 --> 00:52:27,176
Green Grass of Wyoming is a 1948 American Western film directed by Louis King
and starring Peggy Cummins, Charles Coburn and Robert Arthur.

11
00:57:35,294 --> 00:57:41,294
The screenplay, written by Martin Berkeley, is based on the third book in the
popular, "My Friend Flicka" trilogy, written by Mary O'Hara.

12
01:02:49,411 --> 01:02:55,411
The film follows the further adventures of the McLaughlin
family who live on a horse ranch in Wyoming.

13
01:08:03,529 --> 01:08:09,529
Marilyn Monroe appeared as an uncredited extra.

14
01:13:17,647 --> 01:13:23,647
The original cast from the first two films did not
reprise their roles in the third.

15
01:18:31,764 --> 01:18:37,764
The film explores themes of horse, ranch, romance.

16
01:23:45,882 --> 01:23:51,882
The tone is emotional.
